#
# Every test of this module is a compile-time check: a program that
# does not build is the failure (MODULE buildfail FAIL).

assertion  XSH.2.2-compilation-environment.001
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.2.1
class      required
says       Without the feature test macro __STDC_WANT_LIB_EXT1__ (and with it
           defined as 0), headers do not make the Annex K names visible:
           after including the headers, a program can define its own
           objects called fopen_s, fprintf_s, freopen_s, fscanf_s, gets_s,
           printf_s, scanf_s, snprintf_s, sprintf_s, sscanf_s, tmpfile_s,
           tmpnam_s, vfprintf_s, vfscanf_s, vprintf_s, vscanf_s,
           vsnprintf_s, vsprintf_s, vsscanf_s, abort_handler_s, bsearch_s,
           getenv_s, ignore_handler_s, mbstowcs_s, qsort_s,
           set_constraint_handler_s, wctomb_s, asctime_s, ctime_s, gmtime_s,
           localtime_s, fwprintf_s, fwscanf_s, snwprintf_s, swprintf_s,
           swscanf_s, vfwprintf_s, vfwscanf_s, vswprintf_s, vswscanf_s,
           vwprintf_s, vwscanf_s, wprintf_s and wscanf_s, and the macros
           RSIZE_MAX, L_tmpnam_s and TMP_MAX_S are not defined.
note       The names that begin with wcs, such as wcstombs_s, are left out:
           that prefix is reserved for <string.h> and <wchar.h> anyway.
test       t/001-annex-k-hidden.c

assertion  XSH.2.2-compilation-environment.002
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.2.2
class      required
says       Including every header the standard requires of all systems, in
           alphabetical order and each one twice in a row, gives a program
           that builds and whose definitions work (a few well-known macros
           and types from different headers are used together).
note       The headers of options (mqueue.h, spawn.h, XSI ones) and the
           headers that depend on an optional part of the C language
           (complex.h, tgmath.h, threads.h, stdatomic.h) are left out.
test       t/002-headers-forward.c

assertion  XSH.2.2-compilation-environment.003
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.2.2
class      required
says       The same headers in the opposite order, each twice in a row, also
           give a program that builds and works.
test       t/003-headers-reverse.c

assertion  XSH.2.2-compilation-environment.004
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.2.2
class      required
says       After including every header of 002, a program can define its own
           file-scope objects called index, rindex, bcopy, bzero, bcmp, valloc,
           getdtablesize, getpagesize, ulong, ushort, uint, u_char, u_short,
           u_int, u_long, min and max, and none of the
           names MIN, MAX, TRUE, FALSE, MAXPATHLEN, NBBY, howmany, roundup or
           powerof2 is defined as a macro.
note       None of these names appears in the standard, none matches a
           reserved prefix, suffix or complete name of 2.2.2, so no header
           may make them visible. The set is a sample, not the whole
           guarantee ("no other identifiers are reserved").
test       t/004-free-names.c

assertion  XSH.2.2-compilation-environment.005
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.2.1
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With _XOPEN_SOURCE 800 and _POSIX_C_SOURCE 202405L both defined,
           the XSI interfaces are visible (srand48, lrand48, nftw, shmget,
           msgget, semget), so are POSIX ones (strnlen, posix_memalign,
           clock_gettime), and XSI is claimed (_XOPEN_UNIX defined and
           sysconf(_SC_XOPEN_UNIX) greater than 0).
test       t/005-xopen-and-posix.c

assertion  XSH.2.2-compilation-environment.006
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.2.1
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With only _XOPEN_SOURCE 800 defined, all of the functionality
           that _POSIX_C_SOURCE 202405L enables is visible too (strnlen,
           posix_memalign, clock_gettime, O_CLOEXEC, _POSIX_VERSION at least
           202405L) as well as the XSI interfaces.
test       t/006-xopen-alone.c
